Phone LED: a memory-only "dark" hold over ubus, for the LED app's night mode

The phone daemon owns green:phone and reads the level back every step, restoring it when
another program writes it - so the LED app (luci-app-cw-led) cannot put the lamp out at night,
and its night mode had no Phone entry. This adds one ubus method,

    ubus call awvoice indicator_dark '{"dark":true}'    # false lets it follow the line again

which holds the LED dark while the line's state keeps running underneath (a call still rings,
the status reply still says ring). The read-back holds the dark against other writers the same
way it holds a lit level. It is not a setting: nothing is written to /etc/config/awvoice, so the
phone page keeps showing the user's own LED choice, and a restart of the service clears the hold
(the LED app asserts it again on its next tick). Releasing it restarts a blink from its lit half.
tests/test_indicator.c covers the hold, a call ringing under it, another writer, and the release.

Applies to: https://github.com/Pr0Luci/openwrt-aw1000-voice-awvoice.git
